\v 8 You,\f + \fr 1:8 \ft The Alex. MS. omits \fqa You… saved.\f* Oh master, according to your great goodness have promised repentance and forgiveness to those who've sinned against you. Of your infinite mercies, you've appointed repentance to sinners, that they may be saved. You therefore¦114589, Oh master, who are the¦114591 god¦114592 of the¦114593 just¦114594, haven't appointed repentance to the just, to Avraham, Yitshak, and¦114601 Ya'akov, which haven't sinned against you, but¦114603 you've¦114608 appointed repentance to me, a sinner.
\v 9 Because I've sinned more times than there are grains of sand in the¦114610 sea. My transgressions are multiplied,\f + \fr 1:9 \ft The Alex. MS. omits \fqa Oh master… multiplied.\f* Oh master, my transgressions are multiplied, and¦114615 I'm¦114617 not worthy¦114618 to¦114619 look up and¦114620 see the¦114622 height¦114623 of¦114624 heaven¦114625 for the multitude¦114627 of my iniquities.
\v 10 I'm bowed down with many iron bands, so that¦114636 I can't¦114637 lift up my head¦114640 because¦114647 of my sins,\f + \fr 1:10 \ft Some authorities omit \fqa by reason of my sins.\f* and I¦114641 have no¦114643 relief; for I've¦114645 provoked your anger¦114650, and¦114652 done that¦114653 which is evil¦114654 before¦114655 you¦114656:\f + \fr 1:10 \ft The Alex. MS. omits \fqa I did… commandments.\f* I didn't¦114658 do¦114659 your will¦114661, and¦114663 I didn't¦114664 keep your commandments. I've set up abominations, and¦114671 have multiplied detestable things.
