\v 13 but, I¦114702 humbly ask you, forgive me, Oh master, forgive me, and¦114703 please don't destroy me with my iniquities. Don't be angry with me forever, by reserving evil¦114717 for me. Don't condemn me into¦114722 the¦114723 lower parts of the¦114725 earth¦114726. Because¦114727 you¦114728, Oh master, are the god¦114730 of those who¦114732 repent.
\v 14 In¦114735 me you'll show all¦114738 your goodness, for you'll¦114741 save¦114745 me, even though I'm¦114744 unworthy, according¦114747 to¦114747 your great mercy¦114750.
